class.description:
A [PckPackage] holds the file list of a pack. [method PckPackageServer.open] reads it from a [code].pck[/code] file without mounting the pack; [code]PckPackage.new()[/code] creates an empty pack. Files can be added, removed and renamed in memory, and [method PckPackageServer.build] writes the result as a new pack. Reading file data, verifying and building go through [PckPackageServer].
Paths inside a package can be given with or without [code]res://[/code]; they are always listed with [code]res://[/code].
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var package := PckPackageServer.open("user://mods/level_pack.pck")
if package:
	package.add_file_from_buffer("res://levels/extra.txt", "Hello".to_utf8_buffer())
	package.remove_file("res://levels/old.tscn")
	PckPackageServer.build(package, "user://mods/level_pack_v2.pck")
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
PckPackage package = PckPackageServer.Open("user://mods/level_pack.pck");
if (package != null)
{
    package.AddFileFromBuffer("res://levels/extra.txt", "Hello".ToUtf8Buffer());
    package.RemoveFile("res://levels/old.tscn");
    PckPackageServer.Build(package, "user://mods/level_pack_v2.pck");
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] A [PckPackage] is not thread-safe. Use one package from one thread at a time.
